<|channel>thought
================================thought
<channel|>Automated password recovery is the gold standard, but it isn't infallible. When a user loses access to their primary email or their two-factor authentication device, they hit a digital dead end. This is where a manual fallback becomes essential.

By providing a secure way for human administrators to verify identity through alternative documentation or secondary security questions, you prevent permanent account lockout. A manual process acts as a vital safety net, ensuring that a single lost device doesn't result in the total loss of a user's data and history. [end of text]


